Harlequin Town is the settlement toward the front of the [[Org/The Harlequins/Providence|Providence]], the most built-up part of the strider. It runs some four blocks of low buildings whose insides are hard to read from the street. A clock tower stands at its middle, and off to one side of the tower is a building like a cathedral in stone brick and buttresses and stained glass, which is the town's library.

The library carries no device of the six gods, only an eye among four hands above its doors. Inside is one long open room of shelves and desks, a brazier of reaching spectral hands, a silent reading floor, a wall of fire at the back, and a desk where library goods are borrowed. [[Org/The Harlequins/People/Ocelith|Ocelith]] the curator receives readers there, and [[Bestiary/Vermin|zabubs]] fetch the books.

The [[Org/The Harlequins/index|Harlequins]] keep the town in their pinstripes and bell-capped masks. They do not speak to one another; word passes between them in a way like a [[Phenomena/Hearts|Heart's]] skein, and they move and trade places quickly enough that they are hard to count, near fifty in sight at once. Some work at construction and shoring up defenses. [[Bestiary/Fiends|Orts]] are kept about as laborers.
